    private static function setup(string $reason):never
    {
        header('Cache-Control: no-store');header('X-Robots-Tag: noindex, nofollow, noarchive');$b=self::e(self::$base);
        ?><!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>Commerce sandbox setup</title><link rel="stylesheet" href="<?=$b?>/assets/css/commerce.css?v=20261031-phase3"></head><body><main class="commerce-page"><h1>Commerce sandbox</h1><p class="commerce-banner">Administrator preview · Simulated payments only · No email is sent</p><?php if($reason==='disabled'):?><h2>Hosted sandbox is paused</h2><p>The server configuration has disabled this preview. Your administrator navigation entry remains available.</p><p>To resume the preview, remove the <code>COMMERCE_HOSTED_SANDBOX_ENABLED=0</code> override from the hosting environment.</p><?php elseif($reason==='initialize'):?><h2>Your sandbox is ready to initialize</h2><p>Create this installation's Commerce settings, then enable reserved-seat ticketing in Configuration. No account or production data is replaced. Payments remain simulated and purchaser email must use a synthetic .invalid address.</p><?php self::form('bootstrap');?><button>Initialize Commerce sandbox</button></form><?php else:?><h2>One-time database setup required</h2><p>The Commerce files are installed, but its database tables are not ready. Uploading files by FTP does not install database tables.</p><ol><li>Back up the hosted database.</li><li>In your hosting database tool (for example, phpMyAdmin), review and import <code>database/migrations/101_connect_commerce.sql</code>, then <code>database/migrations/102_commerce_simulated_reconciliation.sql</code> and <code>database/migrations/103_commerce_box_office.sql</code>, then <code>database/migrations/104_commerce_storefront_preview.sql</code>, <code>database/migrations/105_commerce_general_admission.sql</code> and <code>database/migrations/106_commerce_discount_snapshot.sql</code>, then <code>database/migrations/107_commerce_performance_schedule.sql</code>, then <code>database/migrations/108_commerce_stripe_test.sql</code> and <code>database/migrations/109_commerce_ticket_delivery.sql</code>.</li><li>Return here and initialize the Commerce sandbox. Enable reserved-seat ticketing in its Configuration screen.</li></ol><p>These scripts add Commerce tables and protective triggers. They do not replace accounts, productions or existing ticket links. If an import has already been partially applied, review the existing tables and triggers before retrying.</p><?php endif;?><p><a href="<?=$b?>/admin/commerce">Check setup again</a> · <a href="<?=$b?>/admin/operations">Back to Operations</a></p></main></body></html><?php exit;
